# lf125, the guarded granary marcher (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf125
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_rowan_eelwater
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the guarded granary marcher
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_old_marching_songs
likes pickled_herring wrestling market_bustle thunder
dislikes waiting night_noise
fears a_stranger_learning_the_house_path a_standing_stone_broken_for_roadwork
hopes a_quiet_watch_on_the_granary a_clear_answer_to_the_old_stones
topics work +0.5 memories +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=spare gossip=guarded refuse=blunt tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# stacks #grain# to the rhythm of an old #march#, guards the #door# against unknown faces, and believes the #stones# remember.

words
oath! = Grain and old stone | By the steady step
saying! = March the sacks in order | A stone keeps more than a book
grain = grain | stored grain
granary = granary | Longmead granary
loft = loft | grain loft
barn = barn | wide barn
sack = sack | grain sack
sacks = sacks | grain sacks
bin = bin | grain bin
bins = bins | grain bins
stack = stack | grain stack
stacks = stacks | grain stacks
sheaf = sheaf | cut sheaf
sheaves = sheaves | bound sheaves
wheat = wheat | dry wheat
barley = barley | field barley
scoop = scoop | wooden scoop
rope = rope | binding rope
knife = knife | work knife
cart = cart | grain cart
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
road = road | long road
path = path | field path
field = field | open field
mud = mud | road mud
boot = boot | work boot
boots = boots | work boots
floor = floor | granary floor
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | farm work
wage = wage | thin wage
price = price | grain price
merchant = merchant | town merchant
market = market | busy market
queue = queue | waiting queue
watch = watch | town watch
city = city | far city
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | closed door
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof
stranger = stranger | unknown stranger
newcomer = newcomer | newcomer to town
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
song = song | old song
songs = songs | marching songs
march = march | old march
step = step | marching step
steps = steps | measured steps
hum = hum | quiet hum
voice = voice | low voice
beat = beat | steady beat
stone = stone | standing stone
stones = stones | old stones
mark = mark | worn mark
marks = marks | worn marks
memory = memory | old memory
secret = secret | kept secret
thunder = thunder | distant thunder
storm = storm | passing storm
rain = rain | heavy rain
cloud = cloud | low cloud
night = night | noisy night
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
day = day | working day
hour = hour | long hour
herring = herring | pickled herring
pickle = pickle | sharp pickle
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | day bread
meal = meal | plain meal
larder = larder | small larder
wrestling = wrestling | green wrestling
bout = bout | wrestling bout
green = green | town green
grapple = grapple | firm grapple
hold = hold | steady hold
crowd = crowd | market crowd
festival = festival | town festival
coin = coin | small coin
bench = bench | wooden bench
table = table | shared table
name = name | given name
houses = houses | great houses
wagons = wagons | unknown wagons
storms = storms | heavy storms

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : The #city# takes a #name# and loses it in a #crowd#. | I prefer a #door# I can close.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : A #queue# can hold a person longer than a #sack# of #grain#. | There is #work# at the #granary#.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : A loose #voice# after drink cannot put its words back. | I keep my accounts sober.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The great #houses# take our #grain# and leave their workers unseen. | I know the #hands# who carried it.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# rises while a #hand# still earns the same #wage#. | I read every mark on a #sack#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 2 : I keep the #door# shut until I know a #newcomer#. | One careless #hand# can leave the #bins# open.
opinion @1 road against 1 : The #road# carries more unknown #wagons# each season. | I would rather keep the #field# in sight.
opinion @1 strangers against 3 : A #stranger# does not need the path to my #home#. | We can speak from the #granary# #door#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #sacks# grow heavier while the #coin# grows thinner. | No one at the #market# calls that fair.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Keep the #door# clear. | #greet#. The #grain# is nearly stacked.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Your #plate# is on the #table# beside mine. | Come hear the old #march# if you wish.
line @1 greet.return : The #bins# are still in order. | You returned before the #wagon# left.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come into the #house#; the #door# is safe. | There is #herring# after the #work#.
line @1 again.open : I was checking the #rope#. | Did we speak of the #stones#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Shut the #door# behind you. | Keep to the #field# #path#.
line @1 farewell.return : The #grain# may be dry when you return. | Another #march# can wait until then.
line @1 react.news : Give me the account in order. | I will hear it after this #sack#.
line @1 react.news.new : No one unloading at the #barn# has spoken of it. | Who stood close enough to know?
line @1 react.news.known : A #hand# spoke of it at the #market#. | You have a different detail.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would count the #sacks# again. | The #wagon# mark may say otherwise.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is hard to hear. Take the #bench#. | I will stop the #work# for a moment.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves the better #plate#. | I can hum a less solemn #song#.
line @1 answer.how : The #grain# is dry and the #roof# holds. | I would welcome a quiet #night#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am moving these #sacks# into the #bin#. | Wait until the #cart# is unloaded.
line @1 ask.how : How much #mud# did the #road# bring you? | Have you heard the #thunder#?
line @1 sympathise : Sit without speaking if you need. | I can bring #bread# after the #cart# leaves.
line @1 reassure : The #stones# have stood through worse #storms#. | We can check the #stack# in daylight.
line @1 decline : At #night# the #granary# #door# must be shut. | That #stranger# may speak from the #road#.
line @1 accept_decline : I hear you; the #door# remains shut. | Then the #sacks# stay where they are.
line @1 thank : You braced the #cart# while I moved the #grain#. | That #herring# was welcome after #work#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was at the #door# already. | The #rope# only needed one knot.
line @1 preclose : The #bins# need their final count before dark. | The #market# noise is carrying this far.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You wrestle like a #sack# tied in the middle. | Your #march# loses its #beat# after three #steps#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #sack# is dry. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #marks#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #bin# shut through #rain#. | Test the #rope# before moving a full #stack#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay with the #wagon# on the #road#. | Close the #granary# #door# at dusk.
scene grain_order
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the #sacks# in order before the #wagon# arrives. | Then no one has to guess which #bin# is full.
b : Does that save time? | Who checks it?
a : At unloading. | I do.

scene dry_sack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A dry #sack# makes a different sound when I set it down. | I put any damp one apart from the #stack#.
b : Can you hear that? | Where does the damp #grain# go?
a : After years of work. | Spread the #grain# to dry.

scene closed_bin
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I close each #bin# before walking to the next. | A careless gap invites #rain# and other trouble.
b : Do you lock them? | Have you found one open?
a : At #night#. | Too often.

scene wagon_mark
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #wagon# #mark# should match the #sacks# it carries. | I count before a #merchant# names the #price#.
b : Do they object? | Can you read every mark?
a : The hurried ones do. | The ones we use.

scene rope_knot
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rope# across a #stack# needs a knot that will release without a #knife#. | I tie it the same way each time.
b : Who taught you? | Does it hold in wind?
a : An older #hand#. | If the cover stays on.

scene granary_floor
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A dry #floor# keeps the lower #sacks# sound. | I sweep it before the #cart# comes in.
b : Is that your task? | What if it is damp?
a : Today it is. | I lift the #stack#.

scene marching_hum
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hum an old #march# while carrying #grain#. | The #beat# keeps my #steps# even.
b : Do you know the words? | Does anyone join?
a : Some. | Only those who remember it.

scene song_without_words
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One #song# has lost its words, but I remember the #beat#. | It comes back when the #barn# is quiet.
b : Where did you learn it? | Can you sing it?
a : From a relative. | Only the tune.

scene standing_stones
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The old #stones# have #marks# worn down by seasons. | I think they remember who passed between them.
b : Can stone remember? | Do you touch them?
a : I cannot prove it. | I leave them alone.

scene stone_mark
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After #rain# a #mark# on one #stone# looks newly cut. | When it dries, the shape withdraws again.
b : What shape is it? | Have you shown anyone?
a : A bend like a #road#. | A close #friend#.

scene pickled_herring
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Pickled #herring# has a sharp taste after a day of dry #grain#. | I eat it with #bread# before the #house# fills.
b : Do you make it? | Do you share?
a : Someone else pickles it. | When there is enough.

scene green_wrestling
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #bout# of #wrestling# on the #green# clears my head. | I prefer a firm #hold# to a loud #crowd#.
b : Do you win? | Who teaches you?
a : Some days. | Practice does.

scene market_bustle
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #market# at its busiest lets me hear every #price# in one place. | When voices turn to #night# shouting, I head home.
b : Do you buy much? | Do you like crowds?
a : Only #herring#. | At a distance.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #thunder# best from under a good #roof#. | The #granary# walls hold the sound for a moment.
b : Does it frighten you? | What about the grain?
a : Not under cover. | I check the #bins#.

scene night_noise
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Noise at #night# reaches through the #window# of our #house#. | I shut it before the #market# empties.
b : Does that help? | Who makes the noise?
a : Most nights. | The last #crowd#.

scene waiting_wagon
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Waiting on a #wagon# leaves the #hands# beside empty #bins#. | I would rather carry #grain# than stand still.
b : Does it arrive late? | Can you do other work?
a : Often lately. | I keep the #floor# clean.

scene unknown_face
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An unknown face asked for the way to my #home# from the #granary#. | I gave the way back to the #market# instead.
b : Were they lost? | Was that unkind?
a : They did not say. | I kept my #door# shut.

story old_march [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I learned an old #march# long before I worked at the #granary#.
  : The words have gone, but the #beat# still carries a #sack# across the #floor#.
  ask : Who taught you?
  b : A useful rhythm.
  : Someone at home; I remember the #voice#.

story rain_mark [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : After #rain#, the oldest standing #stone# showed a #mark# I had missed.
  : By the next #day# it looked faint again.
  ask : What did it mean?
  b : I would remember that shape.
  : I think the #stone# remembers, even if I do not.

story late_wagon [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : A #wagon# reached the #granary# after all the #hands# had gone home.
  : I kept the #door# shut until I could count its #sacks# in daylight.
  ask : Did the driver wait?
  b : A careful choice.
  : They returned at #morning#.

rule @bark_grain
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the #bin# shut. | This #sack# sounds damp.

rule @bark_march
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say That is the old #beat#. | I know another #march# without words.

rule @bark_stones
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Leave the #stone# where it stands. | The #mark# is clearer after #rain#.

rule @bark_door
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Close the #granary# #door#. | I have not met that #stranger#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #grain# is counted. | #greet#. Keep clear of the #door#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #sacks# are still in order. | You remember that old #march#?
dlg @1 resident.job : I move #grain# at #self.workplace#. | I check #bins#, stack #sacks#, and keep the #floor# dry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must close the #bins#. | #saying.capitalize#. Take the #field# #path#.
graft resident.hub
choice What is the tune you hum? -> tune
node tune
say An old #march# without all its words. The #beat# helps me work.
free
choice What do the stones remember? -> stones
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node stones
say I think their #marks# hold the passing years. I cannot prove it.
choice Back to the granary. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #cart# has arrived. | #greet#. I found the right #rope#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will finish this #stack#. | I can visit the #stones# on a quieter #day#.
